# The environment variables this repository reads, what reads each one, and
# where its value is set. Nothing reads this file, and it is not copied whole:
# the values are set in different places, and some in no file at all.
#
# `.env` and `.env.*` are gitignored at any depth, except `.env.example`, which
# is not ignored at any depth. That is why this one holds no value.
#
# SEC-003: secrets live outside source code and are rotated through controlled
# procedures. Nothing here is a credential; some of these name the ones the
# environment supplies.
#
# The ERP has one hosted project: staging, `first-taste-erp-staging`, since
# 2026-10-15. It is rebuilt from `main` only by the owner's run of the manual
# `Deploy to staging` workflow. No production project exists yet (ADR-0018).
# Every value on a hosted project is the owner's to set, one approved action at
# a time (CLAUDE.md §4, §5). The steps cited below are those of
# docs/program/supabase-deployment.md, "Staging, as built".
#
# Starting and rebuilding the local database needs none of these: `supabase
# start` and `npm run db:reset` read supabase/config.toml, which reads no
# environment variable.

# --- the console: apps/console ----------------------------------------------
# Read by apps/console/src/App.tsx, as `import.meta.env`. Vite puts it into the
# bundle when it builds, so anyone can read it: a VITE_ name never holds a
# secret.
#
# VITE_ERP_FUNCTIONS_URL: the edge functions' base address. Unset, the console
# calls the local stack's http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1.
#   Local:   leave it unset. To point the console elsewhere, set it in
#            apps/console/.env.local. Vite runs in apps/console and reads env
#            files there, not at the repository root. Set but empty, it is used
#            as it is, and the console calls its own address instead.
#   Staging: in the Vercel project's environment variables, for Production and
#            Preview, before the first build (step 8). A build without it still
#            succeeds but calls the local stack, so redeploy one built before.
VITE_ERP_FUNCTIONS_URL=

# --- the edge functions: supabase/functions ---------------------------------
# Read by supabase/functions/_deno/serve.ts, once, when each of the twelve
# functions in supabase/config.toml starts.
#   Local:   in an env file outside the repository, passed to
#            `supabase functions serve --env-file`. apps/console/README.md uses
#            ../erp-local.env.
#   Staging: edge function secrets on first-taste-erp-staging, in the Supabase
#            dashboard (Edge Functions, Secrets). A deploy leaves them as they
#            are.
#
# ERP_DATABASE_URL: erp_edge's connection string. Unset or empty, the function
# stops before it answers anything. No migration gives erp_edge a password.
# Locally, give it a throwaway one; on staging, steps 5 and 6.
ERP_DATABASE_URL=

# ERP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS: the browser origins admitted, comma-separated. Each is an
# exact origin: scheme, host and any port, no path, no trailing slash. They are
# compared exactly, so a wildcard matches nothing. Unset, no browser is
# admitted; an entry that is not an exact origin stops the function. Locally,
# the dev server's http://localhost:5173; on staging, the console's Vercel
# address (step 9).
ERP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# --- the edge functions' tests: supabase/functions/_deno/test ---------------
# ERP_TEST_ADMIN_URL: the local stack's database URL, the DB_URL that
# `supabase status -o env` prints. Read by every Deno test there. Set on the
# command line, as supabase/README.md shows; CI's Database stack job does the
# same. The tests refuse a database that is not on this machine, so it is never
# a hosted project's.
ERP_TEST_ADMIN_URL=

# --- the staging workflow: .github/workflows/staging-deploy.yml -------------
# Read by the Supabase CLI in the workflow's steps. Set only as secrets of the
# GitHub environment `staging` (repository Settings, Environments): never as
# repository secrets, and never in a file. The access token reaches every
# project in the Supabase account, the live ones included.
#
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN: from the environment secret of the same name (step 2).
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD: staging's database password, from the environment
# secret STAGING_DB_PASSWORD (step 3). The workflow refuses to run without it.
SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=

# The repository's code and workflows read no other name from outside it. The
# workflows' other names, such as STAGING_REF and NODE_VERSION, are set in the
# workflow files.
